  "description": "How an identifier is compared, by the service (Identifier.java) and by the client library (identifierKey in evaluation/local.ts): every value of an entry of \"same\" reads as its \"key\", every value of \"unchanged\" as itself. An X509_SHA256 value that is a SHA-256 digest (32 bytes) written in hexadecimal (any case, with \":\" between all the bytes or none) or in base64 or base64url (padded or not; the last character as an encoder writes it) reads as unpadded base64url, the form both evaluators compute; anything else is compared as written, and in the registry format makes the entry unreadable. X509_SKI and JWK_THUMBPRINT have one form, unpadded base64url, and are compared as written. IdentifierFormsTest.java and identifiers.test.ts hold both sides to this file.",
